# Tabula

`tabula` is a training scaffold for a tabular foundation model program aimed at surpassing TabPFN-class performance over time.

This repository does not claim to already match TabPFN 2.5. It lays the groundwork needed to get there:

- typed experiment configs
- synthetic episodic pretraining
- supervised finetuning and evaluation
- live Hugging Face and Kaggle data acquisition
- a transformer-based tabular model baseline
- reproducible CLI entrypoints

## Repository layout

```text
src/tabula/
  cli.py
  config.py
  data/
  evaluation/
  models/
  training/
configs/
  pretrain_synthetic.yaml
  finetune_adult.yaml
catalogs/
  kaggle_tabular.json
```

## Quick start

```bash
python -m venv .venv
. .venv/Scripts/activate
pip install -e .[dev]
tabula data auth-check
tabula data hf-auth-check
tabula data list --quality-tier gold --recommended-only
tabula data search-hf --task-category tabular-classification --limit 10
tabula data search-kaggle --tag 14101 --min-usability-rating 0.9
tabula data fetch --dataset home_credit_default_risk
tabula data ingest-kaggle --slug janiobachmann/bank-marketing-dataset --task-type binary --target-column deposit
tabula train --config configs/pretrain_synthetic.yaml
tabula train --config configs/finetune_adult.yaml
```

## Data workflow

The repo supports both curated and live discovery workflows.

```bash
tabula data auth-check
tabula data hf-auth-check
tabula data list --quality-tier gold --recommended-only
tabula data show --dataset amex_default_prediction
tabula data fetch --dataset adult_census_income --output-root data/raw
tabula data prepare --dataset adult_census_income --processed-root data/processed
tabula data materialize --source-type dataset --recommended-only --processed-root data/processed
tabula data fetch --dataset santander_customer_transaction --output-root data/raw
tabula data prepare --dataset santander_customer_transaction --processed-root data/processed
tabula data inspect --path data/raw/santander_customer_transaction
tabula data fetch-hf --repo-id scikit-learn/adult-census-income --dataset-id hf_adult_census_income
tabula data prepare --dataset hf_adult_census_income --processed-root data/processed
tabula data fetch-kaggle --slug janiobachmann/bank-marketing-dataset --dataset-id kaggle_live_bank_marketing
tabula data ingest-kaggle --slug janiobachmann/bank-marketing-dataset --dataset-id kaggle_live_bank_marketing
```

Prepared datasets now emit a stable `schema.json` and generated config so the training loader consumes deterministic preprocessing instead of refitting encoders on every run. The fetch and prepare path now also validates that source columns are flat tabular scalars, infers `target_column` and `task_type` when it can do so confidently, and persists that resolution into the raw dataset manifest for repeatable future runs.

Set `HF_TOKEN` in `.env` when you want authenticated access for gated or rate-limited Hugging Face datasets. The CLI now resolves the token from `.env` first and passes it through the documented `huggingface_hub.HfApi(...)` and `datasets.load_dataset(...)` token hooks.

See `docs/kaggle.md` for the curated Kaggle plan, `docs/sources.md` for live source commands, [docs/data_pipeline.md](C:/Users/AWright/OneDrive%20-%20Kahua,%20Inc/Projects/tabula/docs/data_pipeline.md) for the prepared artifact contract, [docs/architecture.md](C:/Users/AWright/OneDrive%20-%20Kahua,%20Inc/Projects/tabula/docs/architecture.md) for the model/pipeline diagram, and [docs/execution_plan.md](C:/Users/AWright/OneDrive%20-%20Kahua,%20Inc/Projects/tabula/docs/execution_plan.md) for the staged path to episodic training.

## Current scope

The initial scaffold focuses on the infrastructure required for a serious research loop:

1. A configurable tabular transformer that handles numerical and categorical features.
2. Two training regimes:
   - synthetic episodic pretraining for prior-fitting/meta-learning style work
   - standard supervised training for real datasets
3. Evaluation hooks for classification and regression.

## What is intentionally not done yet

- PFN-style Bayesian posterior training objectives
- a large synthetic task library approximating TabPFN priors
- distributed training
- benchmark orchestration across OpenML-scale suites
- calibration and ensembling recipes

Those are the next layers to build on top of this scaffold.
